SUMMARY:Petal to Paper: Paper Chrysanthemum Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us to create lifelike paper chrysanthemums with botanical accuracy!\nJoin paper artist Nancy Lalicon for the “Paper to Petal: Paper Chrysanthemums Workshop.” In this 4-hour session\, participants will learn to create lifelike paper mums using 90g crepe paper. Nancy will guide you through constructing at least one flower in the first half. In the second half\, you will use colourful media to enhance and make another beauty. Take-home instructions and links to a video will be distributed. Discover the art of paper floristry and leave with your own stunning creations.\n \nOptional items to bring:\n \n\n\nVase to keep your floral creation in\nSharp scissors (4”-5”)\nPreferred tools\, such as long nose pliers or wire cutters\nAdditional colouring materials\n\n\nTuesday\, August 11\, 10 a.m. to 2:30 p.m.\nThere will be a 30-minute break for lunch. We recommend bringing a lunch as there are limited options nearby.\n \nPublic $67\, TBG Members $57 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Nancy Lalicon\nNancy Lalicon is a multimedia sculptor specialized in making botanically accurate paper flowers and plants\, and in facilitating workshops for community art organizations and local groups around Toronto and the GTA. From Peonies to Jupiter’s Beard to the Blazing Star\, Nancy has mastered the intricate art of creating environmentally friendly paper replicas; a modern day\, three-dimensional take on botanical drawing.\n \nTrained in the Fine Arts at the University of Victoria and the Emily Carr College of Art in BC\, she received an MFA from Concordia University\, Montreal. Nancy lives in East Toronto with a large family who lovingly tolerate all her studio hours and mountains of flowers and roots.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/petal-to-paper-paper-chrysanthemum-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
