SUMMARY:Free Edwards Summer Music Series: Fullest Flowering
DESCRIPTION:Led by pianist Chris Au\, the extraordinary musicians of Joy of Music perform a gorgeous array of concert pieces brought vividly to life by dancers from the worlds of classical ballet and contemporary dance. The sumptuous White Swan pas de deux is featured alongside new and recent works by esteemed Toronto choreographers Jera Wolfe and Peggy Baker. A concert as lush and bounteous as the garden of Joy of Music’s founder\, Mary Gore. \n\n\n\nHosted in partnership with the Joy of Music \n\n\n\nThursday\, August 13 at 7 p.m.\n\n\n\nFree outdoor concert \n\n\n\nSee the rest of the Edwards Summer Music Series lineup here. \n\n\n\nThis concert is part of the Edwards Summer Music Series\, which showcases diverse\, contemporary talent set within the natural beauty of the garden. Enjoy eight FREE outdoor concerts in the Garden on Thursday nights at 7 p.m. in July and August. General seating is available on a first-come basis. Guests can also bring their own chairs. Concerts are held rain or shine. \n\n\n\nThe Edwards Summer Music Series is generously supported by the Edwards Charitable Foundation and the presenting Sponsor Foresters Financial.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/free-edwards-summer-music-series-fullest-flowering/
LOCATION:ON
CATEGORIES:Edwards Summer Music Series
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/JOM.jpg
