SUMMARY:Epiphytic Branch Terrarium Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun-filled terrarium workshop with an epiphytic twist!\n \nEpiphytic plants are plants that grow on trees. Think of mossy branches in the canopies of lush rainforests covered with ferns\, vines\, and other flora like orchids. Such a sight is truly something to behold as different colours\, textures\, and forms create a harmonious microbiome! During this workshop\, we will teach you how to create your very own epiphytic branch terrarium inspired by these beautiful scenes.\n \nExpand your houseplant horizons by learning a new technique of cultivating plants and construction method blending organic and synthetic materials whilst bringing home a terrarium that will provide your very own slice of rainforest.\n \nThis hands-on workshop is open to all\, no experience is required. Terrarium glass vessels and planting materials will be provided. Please note the terrarium will have a substrate bottom and will focus on the branch component.\n \nWednesday\, August 19\, 6 to 8 p.m.\nPublic $65\, TBG Members $60 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout the facilitators\nVenusRium is a collective founded by two trans women of colour\, Bree Jiang and Mina Heng\, that aims to foster community connection\, especially for BIPOC and 2SLGBTQIA+ people through terrarium-making and plant-based workshops. They welcome all to their space.\n \nBree Jiang (she/they) is a multidisciplinary artist and facilitator based in Toronto. Throughout her arts practice\, she is inspired by queer ecology and finding metaphors for queer and trans expression within nature. Her lifelong awe of nature has translated into a love of creating enclosed ecosystems. Bree has facilitated terrarium-making workshops and spoken about the joys of creating bioactive terrariums\, including with the Garden Club of Toronto and East End Arts. \n \nMina Heng has had a varied career in various disciplines of visual and performing arts. Whether the work was in illustration\, painting\, mural\, fashion\, film\, music videos\, drag performance\, event hosting\, or even public speaking\, she has always maintained a mission in striving for excellence. Her latest passion for plants combines her love of nature\, dioramas\, and miniatures in the form of terrariums and she hopes to make this burgeoning art form accessible for all.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/epiphytic-branch-terrarium-workshop/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Art,Gardening
